From 63bf1e77d4081bdca92265db15387e886c131a86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:06:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] docs: document the gateway error envelope and its codes

List every error the gateway itself produces, with its status and
code, in the gateway README, and drop the note that the 502 and the
recovered 500 were plain text. Record the change in the CHANGELOG.

It is not marked breaking: no released contract described the
plain-text bodies (the README only named the 429 with Retry-After and
the 500, OpenAPI does not describe the gateway's 429, 500 or 502, and
the CLI documentation that mentioned the plain-text 429 and 502 is new
in this release), and status codes and headers are unchanged. The
entry tells clients that read the text to read error.code instead.
The CLI sections of the README, the CHANGELOG and module-mapping now
describe the envelopes and say that only a 404 with the NOT_FOUND
code means a missing resource. Also record the panic log fix and
update the gateway file and test counts in module-mapping.
